# Venat, Heart of Hydaelyn: on turn 1 Bot1 casts Memnite (not legendary: no card), then Isamaru (legendary: Venat draws
# Sol Ring), then Mox Amber (legendary, but the ability triggers only once each turn: no card, a limit no numbered rule states), so its hand is
# empty. On turn 3 Hero's Sundering is refused in the beginning of combat step (sorcery speed, CR 602.5d) and taken in the
# second main phase: {7}, {T} exiles Bot2's Ornithopter and Venat transforms (CR 701.27a) into Hydaelyn, a 4/4 with
# indestructible. At the beginning of combat on turn 5 Blessing of Light refuses Hydaelyn ("another") and puts a +1/+1 counter
# on Isamaru, which is legendary, so Bot1 draws; Isamaru is indestructible through Bot2's turn 6 and not on turn 7 ("until
# your next turn", CR 611.2a). On turn 7 the blessing on the nonlegendary Memnite draws nothing.

